$DATUM 3'-nitro-4-biphenylamine 6.S2 A mixture of 4-iodoaniline (5.38 g, 24.6
mmol), and 3- nitrobenzeneboronic acid (4.1 g, 24.6 mmol) in DMF/H2O (30
mL : 30 mL) was degassed under N2 for 30 min. K2CO3 (13.8 g, 100 mmol)
and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.57 g, 0.5 mmol) were added to the solution. The mixture
was heated to 100 °C for 3 h with stirring. After cooling, the solvent
was evaporated under vacuum to dryness and the residue was treated with
DCM (50 mL) and washed with H2O (50 mL × 2). The organic layer was dried
over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography (SiO2) eluting with hexanes/CH2Cl2 (20:80 to 80:20).
Product 6 as a red solid (4.47 g, 85% yield). 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6, 400 MHz):
δ 8.30 (t, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 8.05-8.00 (m, 2H), 7.67 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H),
7.49 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 6.68 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 5.42 (br, 1H). 13C
NMR (DMSO-d 6, 100 MHz): δ 149.5, 148.5, 142.4, 131.6, 130.2, 127.6,
124.6, 120.1, 119.3, 114.3. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd for C12H11N2O2 [M+H]+
215.0821 found 215.0814.
