$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (method E1) A mixture of boronic acid (5.0
mmol), tert-butyl (2-bromoallyl)(methyl)carbamate (0.9 eq), XPhos (0.06
eq), potassium triphosphate monohydrate (2.0 eq), ethanol (10 mL) and H2O
(5 mL) in a dry microwave vial was degassed using nitrogen gas for 10
mins. In case of 75, SPhos (0.06 eq) and nbutanol were used. Palladium
(II) acetate catalyst (2 mol%) was subsequently added. In case of 82 and
85, boron pinacol ester 80 (1 eq), aryl bromide (1.5 eq), XPhos (0.1 eq),
potassium triphosphate monohydrate (3.0 eq), and palladium (II) acetate
catalyst (5 mol%) were used. The mixture was further degassed for 5 mins
and then sealed with a cap. The reaction was heated at 60 °C for 16 h.
When the reaction was completed, the solvents were removed in vacuo and
the residue was partitioned between EtOAc and H2O. The organic layer was
washed twice with H2O, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated. The
crude product was purified by column chromatography. The pure products.
tert-Butyl (2-(3,4-dimethylphenyl)allyl)(methyl)carbamate (87a) Following
method E1. The title compound was isolated (81%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
Chloroform-d) δ 7.24-7.07 (m, 3H), 5.38 (br. d, 1H), 5.04 (s, 1H), 4.27
(br. d, 2H), 2.76 (br. d, 3H), 2.26 (s, 3H), 2.25 (s, 3H), 1.45 (s, 9H).
