$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-(1,2,2-triphenylvinyl)benzalde(2): 2
(4-Formylphenyl)boronic acid (0.9 g, 6.0 mmol),
(2-bromoethene-1,1,2-triyl)tribenzene (1.7 g, 5.0 mmol), 12 mL of dry
toluene, and 9 mL aqueous of Na2CO3 solution (2.0 M) were placed in a 50
mL round-bottom flask. Pd(PPh3)4 (104.0 mg, 0.1 mmol) was then added and
the mixture was vigorously stirred at 90 °C for 48 h. After cooling to
room temperature, the resulting mixture was extracted with
dichloromethane followed by purification by column chromatography on
silica gel with petroleum ether/dichloromethane (1:1) as the eluent. 1.35
g yellow solid. Yield: 75%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, C2D6OS, 25°C, δ): 9.93 (s,
1H, CH), 7.64 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H, Ar H), 7.22 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H, Ar H),
7.17-7.11 (m, 10H, Ar H), 7.07-7.02 (m, 5H, Ar H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isomers of Pyrene-Imidazole Compounds: Synthesis and Configuration Effect
on Optical Properties
