$DATUM 5,6′-Di(pyridin-3-yl)-3-(E)-styryl-2,3′-bipyridine, MR29071. To a
reaction vessel in a nitrogen atmosphere containing
5,6′-dibromo-3-(E)-styryl-2,3′-bipyridine (13; 0.250 mg, 0.6 mmol) were
added 3-pyridyl boronic acid (185 mg, 1.5 mmol),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium(0) (10% mol), and aqueous Na2CO3
in 1,4-dioxane. Then the mixture was heated to 80 °C until the starting
material was consumed (TLC). After cooling to room temperature, the
mixture was filtered on Celite and washed with CH2Cl2. The aqueous layer
was extracted with EtOAc. Combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4.
Solvents were removed in vacuo, and crude product was purified by
chomatography (ethyl acetate to CH2Cl2/MeOH 95:5), Product as a white
solid (180 mg, 73% yield). Mp: 224 °C. IR (KBr): 3027, 1585, 1451, 1415,
1011, 967, 809, 745, 704 cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 9.29 (d, J = 1.9 Hz,
1H), 9.07 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 8.98 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 8.88 (d, J = 1.9
Hz, 1H), 8.72 (dd, J = 4.9 Hz, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 8.69 (dd, J = 4,8 Hz, J =
1.9 Hz, 1H), 8.41 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 8,24 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 8.18
(dd, J = 7.8 Hz, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 8,02 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7,92 (d, J =
7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.48 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.46 (m, 2H), 7.36 (t, J = 7.8 Hz,
2H), 7,32 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.25 (d, J = 16.6 Hz, 1H), 7.21 (d, J =
16.6 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 154.5, 153.4, 150.8, 150.1, 149.6,
148.3, 148.2, 146.9, 138.1, 136.3, 134.4 (2C), 134.3, 134.1, 133.1,
133.0, 132.9, 132.7, 132, 128.8 (2C), 128.5, 126.8 (2C), 124.7, 123.8,
123.6 120. LCMS(EI): 413.49 [M + H+].
